Z||000000||84fierotrevor||10-05-2001||07:49 PM||||The fiero I bought has a bad engine and the mecainc said that the heads or somthing need to be replaced because it idles to high ?<BR>It wont go below 2000rpm after warming up or anything ! he tried to adujust the thing in the back (idle control i think its called ?)<BR>and it wouldnt go down so he said he would check it futher. Is it really nessicery to have the heads replaced or what do you guys recomend ? sorry im new to fieros and cars this is my first fiero as well as first car.<BR>thanx.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fix||10-05-2001||07:58 PM||||a high idle like that is usually indicative of a bad EGR tube.  It seems to be a pretty common problem on Fieros, so I'd check that out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rick 88||10-05-2001||08:17 PM||||I think your mechanic is trying to make money. If all it is doing is idling fast it's not the cylinder head. Check for vacuum leaks, bad EGR tube, and check for codes stored in the computer.||||reg||1
Z||000003||84fierotrevor||10-05-2001||08:24 PM||||I'm a newbie to cars so i dont know how to check that stuff ? do you think i should just<BR>drive it home then learn how to check those myself ?||||reg||1
Z||000004||84fierotrevor||10-05-2001||08:36 PM||||Ok. i just called the autoshop guy and he said that 2 cylinders need to be replaced<BR>because they had no compresion this guy is like are family mecanic so i dont think he would be ripping me off but i just want to make shure he knows what he is doing.<BR>would two cylinders with no compression make my car idle at 2000rpms ? also he is charging me 300 2 500 bucks to have the two cylnders replaced is that a good price ?<BR>thanks for the help !||||reg||1
Z||000005||fix||10-05-2001||08:59 PM||||that doesn't sound like a bad price, but if I were you I would try to do the work yourself and just drop another motor in there.  Those 4 cylinder motors are disposable. Once they go you're better off just replacing them than fixing them.   Better yet try to find a v6.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||10-05-2001||09:38 PM||||Let's just clarify something at this point.<P>What year is your car and what engine is installed?<P>At a fast idle of 2000rpm is it running smoothly? Since you are able to drive it, does it have any power? Or do you need to get out and push it to get in front of the car next to you? Also, please share a little history on the car if you know anything about it.<P>I would also ask your family mechanic how he is going to replace just two cylinders.<BR>How about it?||||reg||1
